dsh-web-access — a DeepSeek Harness (dsh) port of web-access
==========================================================

This repository is a DERIVATIVE WORK, not an upstream release.

Capability design, browsing philosophy, channel-selection strategy,
site-experience format, and the original Node helper scripts come from:

    web-access v2.5.1
    https://github.com/eze-is/web-access
    Author: 一泽 Eze (Eze) — MIT License

The upstream package declares `"license": "MIT"` in `.claude-plugin/plugin.json`
and states "MIT · 作者：一泽 Eze" in its README, but it ships no LICENSE file, so
the notice in LICENSE here is reconstructed from that declaration with the
original authorship retained. If upstream publishes a LICENSE with different
wording, that wording governs for the upstream portions.

What this port changed (full delta in README.md):

  * The local HTTP CDP proxy and every `curl` call are gone. A CDP client runs
    in the host process and is exposed as native dsh `web_*` tools.
  * The SKILL.md strategy layer was rewritten against dsh's own tool surface and
    registered through `ctx.skills`.
  * Chrome-only path handling was generalized to the whole Chromium family
    (Chrome / Chromium / Edge / Brave / Vivaldi / Opera).
  * Twelve real defects found while testing and re-verifying the port were
    fixed; they are listed in README.md → 「过程中修掉的真实缺陷」.

No upstream file is copied verbatim. The port is a reimplementation against
dsh's own plugin API: the Node helper scripts were replaced by in-process
equivalents, and skill/SKILL.md is a rewrite that keeps upstream's strategy
layer while adapting it to dsh's tool surface.

Upstream is not affiliated with and does not endorse this port.
